# A step that writes a table and reads it back only to check it: the count decides whether `keep` throws and goes no
# further, so the table is where the route leaves its notes, in the codomain (mathematics.md, "A route's domain and
# codomain"; rule 4 of "The closed picture is the pushforward of the fine one"). The route is the module the `bin` runs.
# The library's operations whose result the body names are steps: `const db = new Database(..)`, and
# `const stored = db.prepare(..).get()`, which `db` goes into through the call it runs on.

route clean.cli
step cli.ts/Ledger()
step cli.ts/Ledger.keep
known #125 step cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database()                   # I
step cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get

line entry > cli.ts call
line cli.ts/Ledger() > Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() value
line Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep > Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger.keep value       # keep changes the ledger it runs on (`this.kept +=`)
known #125 line cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() > _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() value      # I
known #125 line Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() value  # I, K
known #125 line _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get value              # I
known #125 line _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value                 # I, then #101
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get > _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get value
known #101 line _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value     # keep checks the count itself
line cli.ts/Ledger.keep > SQLite(notes) own

home Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger() cli.ts
home Ledger@cli.ts/Ledger.keep cli.ts
known #125 home _·db@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/Database() cli.ts/Ledger.keep                          # I
home _·stored@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/get cli.ts/Ledger.keep

# An error is a value (#121, decision 4): `Error(..)` makes it in the arm that raises it, and each border it crosses
# uncaught hands it on, up to the route.
known #138 choice cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1
known #138 step cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1/Error()
known #138 line cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1/Error() > Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1 value
known #138 line Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1 > cli.ts/Ledger.keep value
known #138 line cli.ts/Ledger.keep > Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep value
known #138 line Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep > cli.ts value
known #138 home Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep/?1 cli.ts/Ledger.keep
known #138 home Error@cli.ts/Ledger.keep cli.ts

side entry left
side SQLite(notes) right
# I: a library's constructor whose result the body names (`const db = new Database(..)`) is no step, so `db` is no
#    value; `duckdb.connect(..)` and `Connection::open(..)`, which say the same, are steps.
# #101: a value made in the body and used by the body's own calls has no taker
# K: a value handed through a field reaches no step inside: `new Database(this.path)` hands `this` (#121, decision 1,
#    cause 3: the reader's `held_in` skips `this` even inside an argument)
